# Secrets. Nothing in this group may ever be committed.
#
# A credential that reaches a git history is compromised even after deletion,
# because the object stays reachable in reflogs, forks and clones. The only
# remedy is rotation, so the cheap defence is never committing one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key
secrets/
keystore/

# Go
/orchestrator/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Foundry (M2 onward)
/contracts/out/
/contracts/cache/
/contracts/broadcast/
# contracts/lib is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Foundry dependencies live there as git submodules, pinned to an exact commit. That
# pinning is the point: the contract tests are what demonstrate the Solidity Merkle and
# ballot encodings agree with the Go ones, so a reviewer has to be able to clone and run
# them. Ignoring lib/ left a fresh clone unable to compile, which made the strongest
# evidence in the repository unreachable to anyone but us.
#
# A submodule is also more checkable than a vendored copy: the commit hash says the
# dependency is exactly upstream, with nothing quietly edited.

# Node / React (M8 onward)
node_modules/
/web/dist/
/web/.vite/

# Local tooling
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
/tmp/

# Local runtime data: mock IPFS pins and presigned uploads.
var/
